                <pb facs="0758" n="676" sameAs="frus:frus1925v02/pg676"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.00/1368: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Persia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Amory</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Teheran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-10-30T22:00:00+03:25"><hi rendition="#italic">October 30,
                                1925—10 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 30—4:57
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>75. Demonstrations against Kajar dynasty, which have appearance of spontaneity …
                    have become more wide and frequent. … Course of events may make more difficult
                    position of the American financial advisers.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Amory</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
